<title>UK: UK miner feared dead after RJB pit accident.</title>
<headline>UK miner feared dead after RJB pit accident.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>One miner was missing and two others were in hospital on Monday after the roof caved in at a pit in northern England owned by RJB Mining, a spokesman for the company said.</p>
<p>The spokesman said the missing miner was feared dead. The two injured men were being kept overnight in hospital but their injuries were not life-threatening, he added.</p>
<p>The accident at the pit, which is near Blenkinsopp in Northumberland, happened when a lump of rock fell from the roof and dislodged steel supports.</p>
<p>The mine employs 130 people.</p>
</text>
